<Layout>
	<div class="coreContainer animateBG animate image-bg page cv">
		<Nav />
		<!-- <Arrow /> -->

		<main class="main" role="main">
			<article class="content">
				<div class="introbox">
					<h1 class="top">CV</h1>
					<ul>
						<li>
							Name -
							<a href="/about/" class="bold">Jesus Acosta</a>
						</li>
						<li>
							Email -
							<a href="mailto:jscartas@gmail.com
                                ">
								&#115&#101&#114&#103&#105&#111&#64&#100&#101&#115&#105&#103&#110&#105&#110&#103&#115&#116&#111&#114&#105&#101&#115&#46&#99&#111&#109
							</a>
						</li>
						<li>
							LinkedIn -
							<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jsacosta" target="_blank"
								>www.linkedin.com/in/jsacosta</a
							>
						</li>
						<li class="print-only">
							Learn more -
							<a href="http://www.designingstories.com/about"
								>www.designingstories.com/about</a
							>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<hr class="cv-divider" />

				<div class="bodybox">
					<dl class="cvitems cvitems-general">
						<dt>
							<h1>Profile</h1>
						</dt>
						<dd>
							<p>
								I am a highly committed UI Front-End developer experienced with
								HTML5, CSS (Sass) and JavaScript.
							</p>
							<p>
								With good knowledge of user-centric design principles, I have built
								front-end components for blue chip brand websites including the
								likes of Elle, Esquire, Harper's Bazaar, Cosmopolitan and Good
								Housekeeping Institute, among others.
							</p>
							<p>
								Aware of ever evolving stacks and trends, I have focused my career
								on CSS challenges and constantly building upon my knowledge of
								JavaScript. I have experience with multiple programming languages
								and frameworks like React, ES6, Node, Webpack and jQuery.
							</p>
							<p>
								I have experience on overseeing code quality and manage the work of
								front-end developers across different countries. Always stepping out
								of my comfort zone in order to learn new skills and be of a greater
								asset to the team around me.
							</p>
							<i>
								Currently working as Senior Front-End Developer for Trendstop with
								no availability for new consultancy clients.

								<!-- Available from ... for freelance and contracts on site in London, UK or remotely. -->
							</i>
						</dd>

						<hr class="cv-divider" />

						<dt>
							<h1>Skills</h1>
						</dt>
						<dd>
							<ul>
								<li>
									<b>HTML/CSS:</b> Ten years' industry experience with HTML and CSS,
									developing responsive interfaces for small, medium-size and large
									projects. Use of HTML5 semantic markup and good understanding of
									modern style techniques. Extensive experience of Sass to improve
									design consistency and flexibility.
								</li>
								<li>
									<b>JavaScript:</b> Large experience with vanilla JavaScript and jQuery.
									Working knowledge of React and Webpack.
								</li>
								<li>
									<b>Design:</b> In-depth understanding of design principles on the
									web.
								</li>
								<li>
									<b>Client-side performance:</b> Understanding of code and design
									techniques that can affect page performance.
								</li>
								<li>
									<b>Team player:</b> I am a good communicator and team player. Passionate
									about producing clean and commented code that is easy to maintain.
								</li>
							</ul>
						</dd>
					</dl>

					<hr class="cv-divider" />

					<h1 class="cvitems-general">Portfolio</h1>
					<dl class="cvitems cvitems-specific">
						<!-- first -->

						<dt>
							<h3 class="project-title">
								Trendstop
								<span class="project-date"> <b>~</b> October 2017 - present</span>
							</h3>
						</dt>
						<dd>
							<span class="subitem subitem-ex"
								>Example of: Saas, HTML5, jQuery/Ajax, React and Webpack.
							</span>
							<p>
								Refactoring huge legacy code and setting up modern workflows and
								technologies to build a component oriented basecode.
							</p>
							<span class="subitem subitem-ex">
								<strong>JS Stack:</strong> The role involves extensive use of React and
								Webpack, and learning the basics of Redux.
							</span>
							<a class="project-link" href="https://www.trendstop.com/"
								>Trendstop premium site</a
							>
						</dd>

						<!-- next -->

						<dt>
							<h3 class="project-title">
								CLD Agency
								<span class="project-date"> <b>~</b> June 2017 - October 2017</span>
							</h3>
						</dt>
						<dd>
							<span class="subitem subitem-ex"
								>Example of: Saas, HTML5, jQuery, Twig (PHP templating language),
								Craft CMS and ExpressionEngine builds
							</span>
							<p>
								In close collaboration with designers, I've been implementing web
								interfaces for a number of projects of this marketing agency's
								portfolio.
							</p>
							<p>
								The role required strong emphasis on performance and clean, well
								structured code under extremely tight deadlines.
							</p>
							<a class="project-link" href="https://cld.agency/">CLD Agency</a>
						</dd>

						<!-- next -->

						<dt>
							<h3 class="project-title">
								Hearst UK: Cosmopolitan, Elle, Harper's Bazaar and Esquire (UK
								brands)
								<span class="project-date"> <b>~</b> October 2015 - June 2017</span>
							</h3>
						</dt>
						<dd>
							<span class="subitem subitem-ex"
								>Example of: technical leadership, Saas, HTML5, Twig (PHP templating
								language)</span
							>
							<p>
								During a huge platform migration effort that started on October
								2015, I've been responsible for overseeing the front-end
								implementation of modules and functionality of Hearst European
								sites.
							</p>
							<p>
								Along with the Head of Development, I work directly with Product
								Managers, Project Managers, QA teams and UX designers, helping to
								drive clear communication and development processes that streamline
								delivery and benefits the product.
							</p>
							<span class="subitem subitem-ex">
								<strong>Version control:</strong> The site was locally developed using
								Amazon EC2 instances and the Gitflow workflow.
							</span>

							<ul class="project-list">
								<li>
									<a class="project-link" href="http://www.elle.es">
										www.elle.es
									</a>
								</li>
								<li>
									<a class="project-link" href="http://www.harpersbazaar.co.uk">
										www.harpersbazaar.co.uk
									</a>
								</li>
								<li>
									<a class="project-link" href="http://www.esquire.co.uk">
										www.esquire.co.uk
									</a>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</dd>

						<!-- next -->

						<dt>
							<h3 class="project-title">
								Hearst UK: Good Housekeeping Institute (GHI)
								<span class="project-date"> <b>~</b> June 2014 - October 2015</span>
							</h3>
						</dt>
						<dd>
							<span class="subitem subitem-ex"
								>Example of: ExpressionEngine (EE) build and front-end
								implementation.</span
							>
							<p>
								As the front-end lead, I developed the CSS architecture using Sass
								to ensure modularity. Working along with back-end developers, we
								created the first mobile-friendly build for a product reviews
								website in the UK.
							</p>
							<p>
								The website went live in November 2014 and the final build was
								launched on September 2015.
							</p>
							<p>
								On April 2017, during an internal awards ceremony, the GHI site was
								recognized as the International Website of the Year.
							</p>
							<br />
							<span class="subitem subitem-ex">
								<strong>Key EE add-ons used:</strong> Matrix, Playa, Zenbu, GWcode Categories,
								Low Seg2Cat.</span
							>
							<a
								class="project-link"
								href="https://www.goodhousekeeping.co.uk/institute"
								>www.goodhousekeeping.co.uk/institute</a
							>
						</dd>

						<!-- next -->

						<dt>
							<h3 class="project-title">
								GoLocalise
								<span class="project-date"> <b>~</b> June 2012 - Nov 2013</span>
							</h3>
						</dt>
						<dd>
							<span class="subitem subitem-ex"
								>Example of: content audit, responsive layout, CSS3, HTML5,
								localised design, ExpressionEngine built.</span
							>
							<p>
								GoLocalise website has over 6GB of data translated and organised
								into 9 different languages. Following an extensive content audit, I
								designed responsive layouts and made localised interfaces to serve
								all the languages involved.
							</p>
						</dd>

						<!-- next -->

						<dt>
							<h3 class="project-title">
								Christian. The Law Firm
								<span class="project-date"> <b>~</b> July 2011 - Jan 2012</span>
							</h3>
						</dt>
						<dd>
							<span class="subitem subitem-ex"
								>Example of: responsive web design, HTML5, CSS3, ExpressionEngine.</span
							>
							<p>
								The team at this London-based law firm wanted to be able to maintain
								the content themselves, and in terms of layout, they were keen to
								make it flexible and adaptable to mobile devices.
							</p>
							<a class="project-link" href="http://www.christianlawfirm.co.uk"
								>www.christianlawfirm.co.uk</a
							>
						</dd>

						<!-- last -->

						<dt>
							<h3 class="project-title">
								BBC World Service
								<span class="project-date">
									<b>~</b> October 2005 - August 2011</span
								>
							</h3>
						</dt>
						<dd>
							<!-- <span class="subitem subitem-ex">Example of: web projects coordination.</span> -->
							<p>
								For 6 years I played the role of special projects coordinator which
								involved providing solid concepts on the look and feel as well as
								HTML/CSS prototyping work for the BBC's Latin American presence. I
								dealt with editors, programmers, designers, copy writers and project
								managers with the goal of recreating web content and make it much
								more effective and memorable for online users.
							</p>
						</dd>
					</dl>

					<!-- <hr class="cv-divider"> -->

					<!-- <dl class="cvitems cvitems-general">
                            <dt>
                                <h2>Interests</h2>
                            </dt>
                            <dd>
                                <p>Progressive enhancement as a strategy for web design, web performance, storytelling in
                                    design.</p>
                            </dd>
                        </dl> -->
				</div>
				<!-- / .bodybox -->
			</article>
		</main>
	</div>
